From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:09:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(model): a park counts the ZFS ARC's evictable part as
 memory the copy can take

On a host whose page cache is the ZFS ARC, MemAvailable leaves the ARC out,
though the ARC gives memory back to an allocation that needs it: a park was
refused for its floor with gigabytes of evictable cache beside it (measured
on a node, 2026-11-26: 10.5 GiB evictable in a 14.4 GiB ARC).

The reading now keeps the ARC's evictable part (arcstats' MRU and MFU
evictable data and metadata), and a park is decided on ForParking:
MemAvailable plus what of the ARC can be given back - its evictable part, no
more than its size less c_min, less a margin of 1 GiB - and, under a memory
cgroup limit, no more than the limit allows (the ARC is the host's, it adds
nothing to the cgroup's room). Allocatable is unchanged: a caller that
cannot wait for the ARC does not count it. The backend copying the weights
paces itself on the host's memory, so that the ARC has time to give back.

The refusal's reading says the evictable part and what of it was counted.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
